This is a 0BSD-licensed freestanding runtime library, in a single C file, for
use with GCC or Clang.

It must be compiled as C99 or later, with the same flags as the rest of the
program, but without LTO (-fno-lto), and the program must provide memcpy,
memmove, memset, and memcmp.

Floating point and SIMD are left out unless asked for: define
FREESTANDING_LGRT_ENABLE_FLOAT when compiling it to add everything to do with
floating point, and FREESTANDING_LGRT_ENABLE_SIMD to add what is written with
SIMD instructions. Define FREESTANDING_LGRT_DISABLE_LIBC_FUNCS to leave out the
functions of the C library, those of stdatomic.h and stdbit.h.
